00:27:26.000 --> 00:27:53.000
And the class that got the choice was about 50-50. The class that got the coffee mug, 90% of them kept the mug. The class that got the chocolate bar, 90% of them kept the chocolate bar. So it doesn't make any sense. They should, everybody should be at 50% if the preferences are consistent. So we did that with chimps. And then later with gorillas and orangutans. And around the same time, some other groups started doing similar sorts of things. So another group did it with some other great apes and it's been done with Capuchins.
获得选择权的班级里，大约有一半人选择了交换。而拿到咖啡杯的班级，90%的人留下了杯子。拿到巧克力棒的班级，90%的人留下了巧克力棒。这完全说不通。如果偏好是一致的，每个人都应该有50%的选择比例。所以我们对黑猩猩做了同样的实验，后来又对大猩猩和红毛猩猩做了实验。大约在同一时间，其他研究小组也开始进行类似的实验。另一个小组对其他类人猿进行了实验，卷尾猴也做过同样的测试。

