actual wild capuchin to be doing this? And we can do that in two ways. First, we can do observational studies in our own social groups. And then we can also do observational studies on these groups in the wild. So it's not necessarily a new question per se, but trying to understand how we complete this arc to understand what we're seeing in the lab maps on to what we see in natural environments, which I think is really an important question for understanding how it relates to humans. And along with that, we're trying to get at some of the underlying mechanisms. So Marcella and I've started studying hormones. We've now got an eye tracker. There are lots of things you can do non-invasively with the monkeys' full participation in consent or assent.
